procedure, y = {yi} converge to the local minimum of the energy function.
The energy function of Hopfield networks is also the loss function that is used for training:
LHopfield(ytrain, w) = Fw(ytrain). The training is done by updating the connections w to lower
the energy of data samples:
wi j ←wi j −∂L(ytrain, w)
